---
// Mid-Wilshire-only section: the Metro D Line extension, SB 79, and the Miracle Mile HPOZ. Sources,
// checked October 2026:
// - D Line Section 1 (Wilshire/La Brea, Wilshire/Fairfax, Wilshire/La Cienega) opened May 8, 2026 (LA
//   Metro, The Source). Beverly Hills and Century City stations are projected for spring 2027 and the two
//   Westwood stations for fall 2027; Metro has not set dates, so they are shown as "projected 2027".
// - SB 79 took effect July 1, 2026. LA adopted a phased approach (Option C1) in March 2026 that delays full
//   implementation in historic districts, lower-resource areas, and high fire severity zones until 2030
//   (Councilmember Yaroslavsky's statement, March 25, 2026).
// - Miracle Mile HPOZ: approved by the City Council 13-0 in 2017, roughly Wilshire to San Vicente between
//   Fairfax and La Brea, with some multifamily blocks left out (Larchmont Buzz coverage of the votes).
const stations = [
	{ name: 'Wilshire/Western', note: 'Koreatown', status: 'open' },
	{ name: 'Wilshire/La Brea', note: 'Opened May 2026', status: 'new' },
	{ name: 'Wilshire/Fairfax', note: 'Opened May 2026', status: 'new' },
	{ name: 'Wilshire/La Cienega', note: 'Opened May 2026', status: 'new' },
	{ name: 'Beverly Hills & Century City', note: 'Projected 2027', status: 'future' },
	{ name: 'Westwood', note: 'Projected 2027', status: 'future' },
];
---

<section class="section mw">
	<div class="container mw__narrow">
		<span class="eyebrow">What&rsquo;s New in Mid-Wilshire</span>
		<h2>The Subway Is Here: What the D Line Means for Mid-Wilshire Apartment Owners</h2>
		<p>
			On May 8, 2026, the Metro D Line extension opened three new subway stations along Wilshire Blvd: Wilshire/La Brea, Wilshire/Fairfax, and
			Wilshire/La Cienega. For the first time, a Mid-Wilshire tenant can ride straight to Koreatown and Downtown LA without a car, and by 2027 the
			line is projected to reach Beverly Hills, Century City, and Westwood.
		</p>
	</div>

	<div class="container">
		<figure class="mw-line" aria-labelledby="mw-line-cap">
			<figcaption id="mw-line-cap" class="mw-figcap">Metro D Line along Wilshire Blvd, east to west</figcaption>
			<ol class="mw-line__stops">
				{
					stations.map((s) => (
						<li class={`mw-line__stop mw-line__stop--${s.status}`}>
							<span class="mw-line__dot" aria-hidden="true" />
							<span class="mw-line__name">{s.name}</span>
							<span class="mw-line__note">{s.note}</span>
						</li>
					))
				}
			</ol>
			<p class="mw-source">Source: LA Metro. Dates for the stations west of La Cienega are projections, not set opening dates.</p>
		</figure>
	</div>

	<div class="container mw-cards">
		<div class="mw-card">
			<h3>Put the walk to the station in your marketing</h3>
			<p>
				Renters pay for an easy commute, and buyers price in future rent growth. If your building is within a 10 to 15 minute walk of a new station,
				say so, with the minutes, in the offering. It is one of the few selling points in Mid-Wilshire that did not exist a year ago.
			</p>
		</div>
		<div class="mw-card">
			<h3>Get a zoning check before you set a price</h3>
			<p>
				A new state law, SB 79, took effect July 1, 2026 and allows more housing near major transit stops. Los Angeles is phasing it in, and in
				historic districts full implementation waits until 2030. If your lot is near a station, a developer may value the land more than an investor
				values the building. Print your parcel&rsquo;s zoning from the city&rsquo;s <a href="https://zimas.lacity.org/" rel="noopener">ZIMAS</a> site
				and ask us to price it both ways.
			</p>
		</div>
		<div class="mw-card">
			<h3>Know whether you are in the Miracle Mile HPOZ</h3>
			<p>
				Much of the area south of Wilshire between Fairfax and La Brea is a Historic Preservation Overlay Zone, approved by the City Council in 2017.
				Inside it, exterior changes and new construction go through design review. That matters most to buyers planning to add units or rebuild, so
				your ZIMAS printout should show it either way.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>

	<div class="container mw__narrow">
		<p class="mw-proof">
			Our sale of <a href="/case-studies/1201-s-orange-grove-ave-mid-wilshire-apartments/">1201 S Orange Grove Ave</a>, a 5-unit rent-controlled
			building with structural issues and minimal parking, closed at full price on an accelerated timeline. We have also sold nearby in Arlington
			Heights, including <a href="/case-studies/1513-arlington-ave-arlington-heights-apartments/">1513 Arlington Ave</a>.
		</p>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	.mw__narrow {
		max-width: 820px;
	}

	.mw-figcap {
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-size: 1.15rem;
		color: var(--navy-dark);
		margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
	}

	.mw-source {
		font-size: 0.78rem;
		color: var(--ink-light);
		margin: 1rem 0 0;
	}

	/* Station line diagram: a horizontal subway line on desktop, vertical on phones. */
	.mw-line {
		margin: 2rem 0;
		background: var(--paper);
		border: 1px solid var(--border);
		border-top: 3px solid var(--gold);
		border-radius: 2px;
		padding: 1.75rem 2rem;
	}

	.mw-line__stops {
		list-style: none;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(6, 1fr);
		position: relative;
	}

	.mw-line__stops::before {
		content: '';
		position: absolute;
		top: 11px;
		left: calc(100% / 12);
		right: calc(100% / 12);
		height: 6px;
		background: linear-gradient(to right, #6a3d9a 0 60%, transparent 60%), repeating-linear-gradient(to right, #6a3d9a 0 10px, transparent 10px 18px);
	}

	.mw-line__stop {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		align-items: center;
		text-align: center;
		gap: 0.35rem;
		position: relative;
		padding: 0 0.3rem;
	}

	.mw-line__dot {
		width: 28px;
		height: 28px;
		border-radius: 50%;
		background: #fff;
		border: 5px solid #6a3d9a;
		position: relative;
		z-index: 1;
	}

	.mw-line__stop--new .mw-line__dot {
		background: var(--gold);
	}

	.mw-line__stop--future .mw-line__dot {
		border-style: dashed;
		border-color: #a58cc4;
	}

	.mw-line__name {
		font-weight: 600;
		font-size: 0.88rem;
		color: var(--navy-dark);
		line-height: 1.3;
	}

	.mw-line__note {
		font-size: 0.75rem;
		color: var(--ink-light);
	}

	.mw-line__stop--new .mw-line__note {
		color: var(--gold-dark);
		font-weight: 700;
	}

	.mw-cards {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
		gap: 1.5rem;
	}

	.mw-card {
		background: var(--paper-alt);
		border-top: 3px solid var(--gold);
		border-radius: 2px;
		padding: 1.5rem;
	}

	.mw-card h3 {
		font-size: 1.15rem;
		margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
	}

	.mw-card p {
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		line-height: 1.65;
		margin: 0;
	}

	.mw-proof {
		margin-top: 2rem;
		border-left: 3px solid var(--gold);
		padding-left: 1rem;
		font-style: italic;
	}

	@media (max-width: 860px) {
		.mw-cards {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}
	}

	@media (max-width: 640px) {
		.mw-line {
			padding: 1.25rem;
		}

		.mw-line__stops {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 1rem;
		}

		.mw-line__stops::before {
			top: 14px;
			bottom: 14px;
			left: 11px;
			right: auto;
			width: 6px;
			height: auto;
			background: linear-gradient(to bottom, #6a3d9a 0 60%, transparent 60%), repeating-linear-gradient(to bottom, #6a3d9a 0 10px, transparent 10px 18px);
		}

		.mw-line__stop {
			flex-direction: row;
			flex-wrap: wrap;
			text-align: left;
			align-items: center;
			gap: 0.2rem 0.75rem;
			padding: 0;
		}

		.mw-line__note {
			flex-basis: 100%;
			padding-left: calc(28px + 0.75rem);
			margin-top: -0.2rem;
		}
	}
</style>
